<Base title="Get xNet — early beta" description="The desktop community app is in early beta for macOS, Windows, and Linux."><Nav />
<main id="main-content" class="m-wrap beta-page">
<p class="m-note">Desktop first · Early beta</p><h1 class="m-title">Try the next chapter.</h1>
<p class="m-lede">xNet is becoming a place for private conversations, public posts, music, and video shared by peers.</p>
<p class="m-copy">We’re preparing a small friends beta for macOS, Windows, and Linux. Public signed installers and an update channel are not available here yet. The old Electron downloads describe a different app.</p>
<a class="m-button mt-8" href="https://github.com/crs48/xNet">Build the current app ↗</a>
<section><h2>Before you try it</h2><ul>
<li>Sharing requires an online peer with an authorized copy. There is no server copy of private chat history.</li>
<li>The room owner must be online for new messages. A member may serve history using a permission that lasts up to five minutes.</li>
<li>There is no account recovery or automatic import from the old workspace.</li>
<li>The group protocol does not yet have a forward-secret ratchet. This beta is not ready for highly sensitive conversations.</li>
<li>Development installers may be unsigned. A successful build alone is not a verified installation or update.</li>
</ul><p class="m-copy">Current packaging and testing notes are in the <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/crs48/xNet/blob/main/docs/beta.md">beta guide</a>.</p></section>
</main><Footer /></Base>
